    "reason": "Signals are first cut into 4096-point samples, and the samples are then split 7:3 into training and test sets. This is a sample-level split. The paper does not say whether it is random, and it gives no split by file, bearing, or operating condition. In CWRU each class comes from only a few recordings, so windows from the same recording almost certainly appear on both sides. Coded A as the closest category. The per-load results in Table 5 are within-condition evaluations, not cross-condition splits."
